# ============================================================================
# DEV-ONLY RSA-3072 PRIVATE KEY — pre-encrypted OTA decryption on-device.
#
# This is the key the DEVICE uses at runtime to unwrap the AES-GCM session key
# of a pre-encrypted OTA image (esp_encrypted_img, RSA scheme). It is bound to
# esp_decrypt_cfg_t.rsa_priv_key in main/ota_button.c and embedded into the
# firmware via EMBED_TXTFILES in main/CMakeLists.txt.
#
# NOTE ON NAMING: the matching PUBLIC half (main/ota_decrypt_pub.pem) is what the
# release engineer feeds to esp_enc_img_gen.py to PACKAGE/encrypt an image. The
# device holds the PRIVATE half to DECRYPT. (The esp_encrypted_img 2.7.1 header
# deprecates the old "rsa_pub_key" field name precisely because it was
# misleading — in this scheme the device stores the private key.)
#
#   THIS IS A SECRET.
#   - This file is .gitignore'd and must NEVER be committed.
#   - It was generated for the DEV phase only. Before production, the release
#     engineer MUST replace it with the real RSA-3072 private key whose public
#     half packages the shipped OTA images.
#   - For production, migrate this secret off plaintext flash: use the DS
#     peripheral (CONFIG_PRE_ENCRYPTED_RSA_USE_DS) + eFuse, and enable flash
#     encryption. (ESP32 classic lacks the DS peripheral, so that move implies a
#     chip change.)
# ============================================================================
